<h1>Ghost Box — Spirit Radio — Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="muted">Last updated: October 25, 2026</p>

<h2>Who we are</h2>
<p>Ghost Box — Spirit Radio (Android app <code>com.usefulappz.ghostbox</code>) is developed by Usefulappz™ (Mike Kelley). Contact: <a href="mailto:mikekelleyii.mk2@gmail.com">mikekelleyii.mk2@gmail.com</a></p>

<h2>The short version</h2>
<p>Ghost Box requests <strong>zero permissions</strong> — including <strong>no microphone</strong> and <strong>no internet permission at all</strong> — so the app is technically incapable of recording you or sending your data anywhere. No accounts, no server, no ads SDK, no analytics, no tracking. Everything happens on your device.</p>

<h2>How the app works</h2>
<ul>
  <li>All sound is <strong>generated on your device</strong> — synthesized static swept through a filter, in the style of a spirit-box radio sweep. The app never listens to you or to the room: it has no microphone permission and records nothing.</li>
  <li>The words that surface during a sweep are <strong>random picks from a word bank built into the app</strong>, played over the generated static. Ghost Box is an entertainment novelty, and it says so in the app.</li>
  <li>The timestamped session log is kept on your device only, so you can look back at your own session. It is never transmitted anywhere.</li>
</ul>

<h2>What the app stores</h2>
<p>Nothing of yours is collected or kept by us. Anything the app keeps (such as your session log) lives in the app on your own device; uninstalling the app erases it.</p>

<h2>Permissions, and why</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>None.</strong> Ghost Box requests no Android permissions — no microphone, no location, no storage access beyond its own private space.</li>
  <li><strong>Internet: NOT requested.</strong> The app cannot connect to the internet.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Ads</h2>
<p>This version contains <strong>no advertising SDK</strong>. A labeled placeholder space is reserved in the app for a possible future version; it collects nothing. If an ad-supported build ever ships, this policy and the app's Google Play declarations will be updated first.</p>

<h2>Children</h2>
<p>Ghost Box is a general-audience entertainment novelty with a mild spooky theme. It is not directed at children under 13, and it collects no data from anyone.</p>

<h2>Changes</h2>
<p>If this policy changes, the new version will be posted at this URL with a new "last updated" date.</p>

